    "notes": "A four-layer height blend like terrain's, with layer 4 taking the remainder weight. t17-t20 are the layers' heights (alpha). 18,844 of 37,911 shader-23 materials in 12.1.5 have no runTimeData[0]; what the client samples for a missing height is not known. The simple-lighting programs (14-25) compute the same diffuse and no emissive. The emissive output is before the client's view-depth fade: after lighting it is scaled by saturate(v5.z * cb1[8].x + cb1[8].y) (SHADER_FINDINGS/notes/wmo.md). Alpha is what the shader alpha-tests (128/255, per MSAA sample)."
